  "limitations": "This does not complete MR-10 or the 17-package goal. Three new component tests cover same/higher-term vote behavior, coherent old image/checkpoint retention across restart, late completion refusal, joining an older physical apply, duplicate completion refusal during held sync, retry installation under a fresh ticket, irreversible install cancellation refusal, and failed abort sync without progress/acknowledgement. They do not implement or qualify native checkpoint scheduling, bulk snapshot RPCs, transfer lifecycle/admission, host publication/readiness, authorized replacement-member S3/peer seeding, missing-quorum normal activation refusal or the native recovery crash matrix. Automatic compaction and native incoming snapshot handling remain disabled. Historical transport fixtures hold mechanical snapshot completions; physical snapshot/SQLite installation is separately exercised. The full-image archive fixture uses the in-memory object-store adapter and mechanically seeds a verified 64-MiB SQLite image; it does not establish a 64-MiB SDK command envelope. Independent snapshot/current/private/apply generation admission and Blob/effect dependency closure still require native integration. Process kill and injected sync failure do not establish physical power-loss behavior. No physical S3, zones, production capacity/performance, larger cluster scale or full release qualification is claimed. Node qualification is the single affected public Raft lifecycle case; the earlier physical record pins its separate 88-case run. Seven ignored child entry points are invoked by owning parents and excluded. Existing vendored warnings remain visible.",
